    {
      "extraction_class": "NORM",
      "extraction_text": "En cualquier caso, en soportes de pared no delgada (clases 1,2 o 3), la capacidad resistente de cálculo considerando pandeo de un elemento sometido a flexocompresión puede verificarse, a partir de las solicitaciones obtenidas de la combinación de acciones en caso de incendio, mediante las expresiones generales de DB-SE-A usando los valores modificados dados a continuación: el límite elástico se reducirá multiplicándolo por el coeficiente ky, de la tabla D.2 como longitud de pandeo se tomará, en estructuras arriostradas y si el sector de incendio no abarca más de una planta, la mitad de la altura entre plantas intermedias, o el 0,7 de la altura de la última planta. como curva de pandeo se utilizará la curva c, con independencia del tipo de sección transversal o el plano de pandeo. la esbeltez reducida se incrementará multiplicándola por el coeficiente k ,  de la tabla D.2",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "c7d8e9f0-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678",
        "parent_section_id": "a45665279d8a1a14",
        "paragraph_number": 3,
        "obligation_type": "MANDATORY",
        "norm_statement": "For non-thin-walled supports (classes 1, 2 or 3), the design resistance capacity considering buckling of a flexo-compressed element can be verified, based on the stresses obtained from the combination of actions in case of fire, using the general expressions of DB-SE-A with the following modified values: the yield strength will be reduced by multiplying it by the coefficient ky,θ from Table D.2; the buckling length will be taken as half the height between intermediate floors, or 0.7 of the height of the last floor, for braced structures and if the fire sector does not cover more than one floor; buckling curve c will be used, regardless of the type of cross-section or buckling plane; the reduced slenderness will be increased by multiplying it by the coefficient kλ,θ from Table D.2.",
        "applies_if": "SUPPORT.WALL.THICKNESS != 'THIN' AND SUPPORT.CLASS IN ['1', '2', '3']",
        "satisfied_if": "DB_SE_A.GENERAL_EXPRESSIONS.VERIFIED == TRUE AND YIELD_STRENGTH == (YIELD_STRENGTH_ORIGINAL * TABLE_D2.KY_THETA) AND (BUCKLING_LENGTH == (INTERMEDIATE_FLOOR.HEIGHT / 2) OR BUCKLING_LENGTH == (LAST_FLOOR.HEIGHT * 0.7)) AND BUCKLING_CURVE == 'C' AND REDUCED_SLENDERNESS == (REDUCED_SLENDERNESS_ORIGINAL * TABLE_D2.KL_THETA)",
        "exempt_if": "FALSE",
